---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
---
<Base title="Set up FieldADE" description="How to install FieldADE on your iPhone, pair it with HomeADE, and start a chat. Includes phone-only setup with no Mac.">
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: calc(var(--header-h) + 2rem)">
    <div class="wrap guide">
      <h1>Set up FieldADE</h1>
      <p>FieldADE is the iPhone app. It shows what is due, your mail, and a chat with the assistants on your Mac. Pair it with <a href="/homeade">HomeADE</a>, which has to be running on that Mac. If HomeADE is not installed yet, <a href="/homeade/setup">set up the Mac first</a>. Pairing takes a few minutes once the Mac shows a code.</p>
      <p><a href="/fieldade">About FieldADE</a></p>

      <h2>What you need</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>An iPhone with iOS 17 or later.</li>
        <li>HomeADE on a Mac, with a pairing code on the screen. Or skip the Mac and <a href="#no-mac">use the phone on its own</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="phone">1. Install FieldADE</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/fieldade/id6828288883" rel="noopener">Install FieldADE from the App Store</a>.</li>
        <li>Open FieldADE.</li>
      </ol>

      <p>A new user sees a <strong>Get started</strong> card on the Today screen. It has four rows: <strong>Machine</strong>, <strong>Vault</strong>, <strong>Agents</strong>, and <strong>Connectors</strong>. Each row has one button that opens the screen for that job. The card counts your progress, for example "1 of 4," until all four are done or you tap <strong>Hide</strong>. <strong>Settings → Get started</strong> brings it back.</p>

      <h2 id="pair">2. Machine</h2>
      <p>The machine is the computer that runs HomeADE. Pair the phone with it, or <a href="#no-mac">use the phone alone</a>.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>On the Mac, HomeADE's window should show a pairing code. If it does not, click the antenna icon and choose <strong>Pair a phone…</strong>. The <a href="/homeade/setup">HomeADE setup</a> gets you to that window.</li>
        <li>In FieldADE, open <strong>Settings → Machines</strong> and tap <strong>Scan a pairing code</strong>.</li>
        <li>Point the camera at the code on your Mac.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>The code holds your Mac's key, so do not share it or post a picture of it. If the phone cannot scan, click <strong>Copy the link instead</strong> on the Mac, send the link to the phone, and tap <strong>Paste a pairing link</strong>. You can also enter the Mac's address by hand. The link asks before it applies.</p>
      <p>The phone reaches the Mac through relay.embry.dev, so it works away from home with nothing else to install. The traffic is encrypted with a key that only your phone and your Mac hold. See the <a href="/fieldade/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="vault">3. Vault</h2>
      <p>A vault is a folder of notes. If you have none, tap <strong>Create a vault</strong>, or open <strong>Settings → Choose sources → Vault</strong>, pick your Mac, and tap <strong>Create a vault on &lt;machine&gt;…</strong> (your Mac's name shows there). The app asks where to put it, then asks for a name. The default is "My Vault."</p>
      <p>The app fills the vault with Ingest, Projects, Areas, Resources, Archive, Zettelkasten, Journal, Outbox, System, and Templates. It adds a Welcome note, a "Getting started" project with three to-dos, and a "Home" area. The vault is plain Markdown, so Obsidian is not needed. To use an existing folder, tap <strong>Choose a folder</strong>.</p>

      <h2 id="agents">4. Agents</h2>
      <p>Chats run in the official Claude Code, Codex, or Grok tool on your Mac. The app never holds their logins. Open <strong>Settings → Machines</strong>, pick your Mac, and tap <strong>Agents on &lt;machine&gt;</strong>. Each tool shows as installed or not, and signed in or not. Sign in to at least one.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Tap <strong>Install</strong> for a missing tool. Install needs Node.js. On a Mac, install Node from nodejs.org or with Homebrew, then tap <strong>Check again</strong>.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Sign in</strong>. A terminal opens that is already running that tool's own login. Finish the login there.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Check again</strong>.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="connectors">5. Connectors</h2>
      <p>Connectors are optional. Tap <strong>Skip for now</strong> to leave them for later. To add one, open <strong>Settings → Choose sources → Connectors</strong>. Rows for Mail, Calendars, and Tickets show a state and, when something fails, a one-line fix. Tap <strong>+ Add</strong> to choose Gmail, Cloudflare, Google Calendar, or iCloud, or Jira, Yahoo, Fastmail, AOL, any other IMAP mail, and more.</p>
      <p>Mail uses an app password. For Gmail, make one at myaccount.google.com/apppasswords. For iCloud, go to account.apple.com, then <strong>Sign-In and Security → App-Specific Passwords</strong>. For calendars, sign in to Google or iCloud on the phone, or allow access to the calendars on the phone.</p>

      <h2 id="first-chat">6. Start a chat</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>On the phone, tap <strong>+</strong> and pick a folder for the chat.</li>
        <li>Type a question about your notes and send it.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Before the assistant edits a file or runs a command, the phone asks you to allow or deny it. The same chat is open in the HomeADE window when you sit down at the Mac.</p>

      <h2 id="more">Add more</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Share sheet.</strong> Share a photo, file, or link to FieldADE and it lands in your vault's Inbox. Items shared while the Mac is away wait on the phone.</li>
        <li><strong>Widget.</strong> On iOS 26 or later, add the FieldADE widget to the home screen.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="no-mac">Without a Mac</h2>
      <p>FieldADE can run on its own. In the Machine row, tap <strong>Use the phone alone</strong>. For a vault, tap <strong>Create my phone vault</strong>, and enter an Anthropic API key. Chats then run on the phone and bill that key. To look around first, tap <strong>Try the sample vault</strong> on the Today screen.</p>

      <h2 id="windows">Windows</h2>
      <p>The Windows build is HomeADE, and the beta cannot pair a phone yet. <a href="/homeade/setup#windows">Windows setup</a> covers the installer and the warning Windows shows.</p>

      <h2 id="trouble">If something goes wrong</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The phone says to set the Mac's address.</strong> The phone is not paired. Do step 2.</li>
        <li><strong>The phone says "no end-to-end key."</strong> Make a new pairing code on the Mac and scan it again.</li>
        <li><strong>An agent says it is not signed in.</strong> Open <strong>Settings → Machines</strong>, pick your Mac, and tap <strong>Agents on &lt;machine&gt;</strong>. Tap <strong>Sign in</strong>, finish the login in the terminal, then tap <strong>Check again</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>You have no vault yet.</strong> Tap <strong>Create a vault</strong> on the Get started card.</li>
        <li><strong>Chats do not start.</strong> Check that one agent is signed in. Then, on the Mac, click <strong>Restart HomeADE…</strong> in the menu. <a href="/homeade/setup#trouble">HomeADE troubleshooting</a> covers a window that says it has no token.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Still stuck? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

